IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `isl-nouns`
IMPORT `isl-p5-duties`

-- Tests for Chapter 5, Sub-chapter C (ss 17(b), 19 to 21A) and the Fifth Schedule.  Expected values are worked out by hand from the text, beside each assertion.
-- The #TRACE runs at the end print the result of each regulative rule.  The stable binary cannot assert on a trace, so the expected result is in the comment above each run and
-- is checked by reading the output (NOTES.md, "What the stable binary does not accept"); the decision-function twins above are the asserted copies.

§ `s 17(b) -- the duty to help, as a decision function`
#ASSERT `s 17(b) the recipient is in breach of the duty` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17(b) the recipient is in breach of the duty` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17(b) the recipient is in breach of the duty` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17(b) the recipient is in breach of the duty` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 19 -- the claimant's duty`
-- arguments: demanded information, demanded an examination, demanded an appearance, has complied
#ASSERT `s 19(a) the claimant or recipient has met the Institute's demand` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 19(a) the claimant or recipient has met the Institute's demand` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19(a) the claimant or recipient has met the Institute's demand` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19(a) the claimant or recipient has met the Institute's demand` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19(a) the claimant or recipient has met the Institute's demand` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 19(a) the claimant or recipient has met the Institute's demand` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 19(b) the Institute may delay the claim, stop payment or refuse the benefit` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19(b) the Institute may delay the claim, stop payment or refuse the benefit` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 19(b) the Institute may delay the claim, stop payment or refuse the benefit` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 20 -- the 60 days`
-- arguments: the change is of the kind, it may affect entitlement or rate, the days from the change to the written notice (if any), the days since the change
#ASSERT `s 20 the recipient notified the change in time` FALSE TRUE (JUST 10) 10 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20 the recipient notified the change in time` TRUE FALSE (JUST 10) 10 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20 the recipient notified the change in time` TRUE TRUE (JUST 0) 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20 the recipient notified the change in time` TRUE TRUE (JUST 59) 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20 the recipient notified the change in time` TRUE TRUE (JUST 60) 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20 the recipient notified the change in time` TRUE TRUE (JUST 61) 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no notice yet: still open on day 60, over on day 61
#ASSERT `s 20 the recipient notified the change in time` TRUE TRUE NOTHING 60 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20 the recipient notified the change in time` TRUE TRUE NOTHING 61 EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 21 -- the duties of a person questioned, and of one who holds information`
#ASSERT `s 21(b) the person met the duty to answer` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(b) the person met the duty to answer` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21(b) the person met the duty to answer` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21(b) the person met the duty to answer` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- arguments: the person has the information, an authorised employee demanded it, the days from the demand to giving it (if given), the days since the demand
#ASSERT `s 21(c) the person gave the details in time` FALSE TRUE (JUST 5) 5 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 21(c) the person gave the details in time` TRUE FALSE (JUST 5) 5 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 21(c) the person gave the details in time` TRUE TRUE (JUST 30) 40 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(c) the person gave the details in time` TRUE TRUE (JUST 31) 40 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21(c) the person gave the details in time` TRUE TRUE NOTHING 30 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 21(c) the person gave the details in time` TRUE TRUE NOTHING 31 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a): the power to enter, and the limit on force
#ASSERT `s 21(a) the employee may enter the place` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(a) the employee may enter the place` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 21(a) the employee may enter the place` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 21(a) the employee may enter the place` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 21(a) the employee may enter the place` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 21(a) the employee may enter by force` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 21(a) the employee may enter by force` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21(a) the employee may enter by force` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 21A(1) the Institute may use the information` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21A(1) the Institute may use the information` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 21A(1) the Institute may use the information` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 21A(2) the provisions of s 326(g) of the Insurance Law apply` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21A(2) the provisions of s 326(g) of the Insurance Law apply` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 20A and 20B`
#ASSERT `s 20A the provisions of s 327 of the Insurance Law apply to the person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20A the provisions of s 327 of the Insurance Law apply to the person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20B(a) the claimant is liable to a fine` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20B(a) the claimant is liable to a fine` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20B(a) the claimant is liable to a fine` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b)(3): sent on 1 March 2026; served on the 15th day after it was sent.  Arguments: sent by registered mail to both addresses, the day sent, the day asked about, the addressee proves non-receipt
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(3) the notice is deemed served` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 30 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(3) the notice is deemed served` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(3) the notice is deemed served` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(3) the notice is deemed served` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 17 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(3) the notice is deemed served` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 30 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(4) paragraph (1) applies to the recipient all the same` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(4) paragraph (1) applies to the recipient all the same` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(4) paragraph (1) applies to the recipient all the same` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(2) the notice meets the content requirements` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(2) the notice meets the content requirements` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(2) the notice meets the content requirements` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(2) the notice meets the content requirements` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(2) the notice meets the content requirements` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(5) subsection (b) does not apply to the recipient` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(5) subsection (b) does not apply to the recipient` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(5) subsection (b) does not apply to the recipient` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b)(1): the notice was sent on 1 March 2026.  Arguments: got such a notice, the day sent, the day of the change, the day the change was reported (if it was), the day asked about
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(1) the recipient is liable to a fine` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) NOTHING (Date 1 9 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a change before the notice, or after four years from it, is outside the paragraph
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(1) the recipient is liable to a fine` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 28 2 2026) NOTHING (Date 1 9 2030) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(1) the recipient is liable to a fine` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2030) NOTHING (Date 1 9 2030) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(1) the recipient is liable to a fine` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2030) NOTHING (Date 1 9 2030) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the change on 1 April 2026: reporting by 31 May 2026 (60 days later) is in time
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(1) the recipient is liable to a fine` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) (JUST (Date 31 5 2026)) (Date 1 9 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(1) the recipient is liable to a fine` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) (JUST (Date 1 6 2026)) (Date 1 9 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- never reported: the 60 days run out after 31 May 2026
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(1) the recipient is liable to a fine` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) NOTHING (Date 31 5 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20B(b)(1) the recipient is liable to a fine` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) NOTHING (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `The Fifth Schedule`
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A note what the basic amount is` EQUALS "the amount in para (3) of the definition of basic amount in s 1 of the Insurance Law -- בפסקה (3) להגדרה ”הסכום הבסיסי“ בחוק הביטוח"
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A the number of the detail` `the balance of an account at a financial institution` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A the number of the detail` `a right in real estate` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A the number of the detail` `income from work` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A the number of the detail` `income from other sources` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A the number of the detail` `the address of residence` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A the number of the detail` `foreign citizenship` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A the number of the detail` `entering and leaving Israel, and time spent abroad` EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A the number of the detail` `living under one roof with a spouse or one of the other persons item 8 lists` EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A the number of the detail` `money received directly from the maintenance debtor` EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A the number of the detail` `a maintenance judgment later than the one given to the Institute` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `sch 5 part B the detail is required` `the balance of an account at a financial institution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part B the detail is required` `a right in real estate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part B the detail is required` `income from work` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part B the detail is required` `income from other sources` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part B the detail is required` `the address of residence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part B the detail is required` `foreign citizenship` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part B the detail is required` `entering and leaving Israel, and time spent abroad` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part B the detail is required` `living under one roof with a spouse or one of the other persons item 8 lists` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part B the detail is required` `money received directly from the maintenance debtor` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part B the detail is required` `a maintenance judgment later than the one given to the Institute` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- items 1, 3, 4: a basic amount of 1,000 makes the thresholds 90 (an individual) and 130 (with a child or a spouse)
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A item 1 the account balance must be reported` 1000 TRUE 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A item 1 the account balance must be reported` 1000 FALSE 91 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A item 1 the account balance must be reported` 1000 FALSE 90 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A item 1 the account balance must be reported` 1000 FALSE 130 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A item 1 the account balance must be reported` 1000 FALSE 131 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A item 3 the income from work must be reported` 1000 TRUE 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A item 3 the income from work must be reported` 1000 FALSE 91 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A item 3 the income from work must be reported` 1000 FALSE 90 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A item 3 the income from work must be reported` 1000 FALSE 130 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A item 3 the income from work must be reported` 1000 FALSE 131 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A item 4 the income from other sources must be reported` 1000 TRUE 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A item 4 the income from other sources must be reported` 1000 FALSE 91 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A item 4 the income from other sources must be reported` 1000 FALSE 90 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A item 4 the income from other sources must be reported` 1000 FALSE 130 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A item 4 the income from other sources must be reported` 1000 FALSE 131 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A item 8 living with the person must be reported` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A item 8 living with the person must be reported` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A item 8 living with the person must be reported` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A item 8 living with the person must be reported` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part A item 8 living with the person must be reported` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 5 part C the warning the notice must carry` EQUALS "הרינו להביא לידיעתך כי אם לא תעדכן את המוסד לביטוח לאומי על כל שינוי שיחול באחד או יותר מהפרטים המפורטים בהודעה זו בתוך שישים ימים ממועד השינוי, במהלך ארבע שנים ממועד משלוח הודעה זו, הנך צפוי לעונשים הקבועים לפי החוק, לרבות קנס; ככל שחל שינוי בפרטים האמורים לגביך אנא עדכן את המוסד לביטוח לאומי בטופס המצורף."

§ `The regulative rules, run with #TRACE (printed, not asserted)`
-- s 20: a written notice on day 60 is in time.  Expected result: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 20 the recipient must report a change` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the claimant or benefit recipient` DOES `notify the Institute in writing of the change` AT 60
-- s 20: nothing by day 61.  Expected result: DEONTIC BREACHED, BECAUSE "the change was not notified to the Institute in writing within 60 days (s 20)".
#TRACE `s 20 the recipient must report a change` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 61)
-- s 20: a written notice on day 61.  Expected result: DEONTIC BREACHED (the act came after the deadline).
#TRACE `s 20 the recipient must report a change` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the claimant or benefit recipient` DOES `notify the Institute in writing of the change` AT 61
-- s 21(c): the details given on day 30 are in time.  Expected result: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 21(c) the person with the information must give it` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a person who has information about the income or property of a claimant or recipient` DOES `give the Institute every detail about the income or property` AT 30
-- s 21(c): nothing by day 31.  Expected result: DEONTIC BREACHED, BECAUSE "the details were not given within 30 days of the demand (s 21(c))".
#TRACE `s 21(c) the person with the information must give it` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 31)
-- s 19(a): compliance at any time.  Expected result: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 19(a) the claimant or recipient must comply with the Institute's demand` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the claimant or benefit recipient` DOES `comply with the Institute's demand` AT 400
-- s 19(a): nothing happens.  Expected result: the obligation printed back (no deadline, so it does not lapse).
#TRACE `s 19(a) the claimant or recipient must comply with the Institute's demand` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)
-- s 21(b): an answer.  Expected result: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 21(b) the person questioned must answer` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a person questioned or whose premises are inspected` DOES `answer every question put, fully and truthfully` AT 3
-- s 17(b), first limb: help given.  Expected result: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 17(b) the recipient must help the Institute` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the claimant or benefit recipient` DOES `help the Institute and take every reasonable step to enable it to realise its right` AT 10
-- s 17(b), second limb: the prohibited act.  Expected result: DEONTIC BREACHED.
#TRACE `s 17(b) the recipient shall not harm the Institute's right` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the claimant or benefit recipient` DOES `do an act liable to harm or prevent the realisation of the Institute's right` AT 5
